WEBVTT

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:28.570
Here kitty kitty kitty.

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:30.340
Hey yo. Walk faster.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.600
Fuck, that hurt!

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.370
Damn you, geezer!

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.750
You're so fucking dull.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:51.600
Colors.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:58.850
The world has many colors.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:05.990
New colors are created

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:12.630
when the old stain, dye and blend.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:17.960
Some colors overlap and melt together.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:22.430
Some colors continue to sink deep.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.190
Distractions day after day, it's always something

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.190
Meutsuri Shiteru Hibi Are Kore

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:58.330
and no one has even realized that

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:03.350
I see the crimson trailing down your cold skin

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:03.350
Awadatsu Hada wo Tsutai Ochiru CRIMSON

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:07.540
Why do you want another punishment?

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:07.540
Why do you want Atarashii Batsu wo

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:12.290
The sweet fragrances that are drifting about

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:12.290
Tadayou Amai Kaori wo Tada

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.850
I just want to leave them be

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.850
Asobasete Itai Dake Nano sa

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:24.530
Someone hurry up and shoot me

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:24.530
Dareka Boku wo Hayaku Uchinuite yo

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:29.680
Show me a gunshot strong enough to make a hole

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:29.680
Show me Kantsuushita Juusou Ana ga Aku Hodo

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:34.150
I crush my thorny grip

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:34.150
Toge Darake no GRIP Nigiritsubushite

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:39.920
and load bullets that look like ripe flowerbuds

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:39.920
Osanai Mada Tsubomi no You na Dangan de

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:44.030
Let me shoot through the soul

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:44.030
Let me, shot through the soul

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:48.980
and dye it rose

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:48.980
Bara-iro ni Somare

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:14.060
Found ya, Akira!

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.020
Rin?

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.150
I'm outta breath.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:22.890
Were you looking for me?

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:27.710
Yeah. It didn't seem like you were going to come back.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.230
Everything go okay?

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:31.250
Yeah, I'm done.

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:33.460
So you can finally stop for a moment?

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:34.740
But seriously.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:37.790
Didn't I already tell you not to get involved in anything that'd make the Executioners chase after you?!

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:39.830
Let's go, Akira!

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:41.690
What? To where?

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:45.130
For crying out loud, you really weren't listening, were you?

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.660
Didn't I say already that we're heading towards the hotel in the Neutral Zone?

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:49.290
The Neutral Zone?

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.790
Yup. It's like that one club we went to before.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.550
That's where we'll rendezvous with Keisuke, too.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:03.140
Jeez, I'm already tired.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.150
Keisuke knows where the hotel is too?

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.540
I did want to stop him though.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:10.010
He said that he wanted to help
search for you since he was worried

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:12.480
about what sort of trouble you may have gotten into.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.060
Won't he be the one in danger?

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:19.260
Well, he should be fine while it's still bright outside.

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:32.400
About that, you see, he-- Huh?

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.070
Hey, that's...

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:39.650
Isn't that Rin?

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.950
He really did come over to Toshima, eh?

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:48.350
Tomoyuki.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:52.350
Yo.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.490
Been a while, hasn't it, Rin?

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:58.930
Hmm, you've found yourself a partner here already, huh?

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:02.850
What is it?

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:06.700
Ain't he pretty?

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:10.010
Well well, you can be friends with me too.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.450
Wow Rin, you're usually really hyper.

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:18.260
Why're you being so silent now?

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.830
That shit isn't cute!

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:22.320
Shut up.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.580
Who the hell do you think you are?

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:35.800
Selling out your friends and running
away isn't something to be proud of!

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:21.040
I'm sorry, Akira.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.450
You know, about what happened earlier...

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:28.690
That? No problem.

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.240
You're not going to ask about it?

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:31.680
Not really.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:35.090
Well, I suppose you wouldn't.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:40.060
If you don't want to talk about it, then don't.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.370
Ah, jeez...

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:50.640
I'm like mega lame now, aren't I?

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:03.980
Come on, hurry up!

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:06.600
Keisuke will go bald if he worries too much!

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.520
Yo. You guys took your time.

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:11.060
Why're you here, gramps?

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:13.310
Where's Keisuke?

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:16.150
He said that he'd go run
around the area one more time.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:18.570
So I'm here to tell you that in his place.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:21.970
That Keisuke...

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:25.210
I'll go look for him.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.580
He was really, really worried about you, you know.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.480
Ah, he's back.

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:40.720
Akira!

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.350
Thank goodness!

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:45.550
You're okay!

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.660
Ah, you're not hurt, are you?

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:50.750
Good job.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:55.300
Did everything go alright?

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:58.110
I was really surprised when you suddenly got dragged away.

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:01.210
Yeah. Rin told me that.

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:05.280
I-I'm sorry, Akira.

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:08.990
About?

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:11.190
T-That I...

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:15.200
I wasn't able to find you after all...

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.660
Don't be hard on yourself.

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:21.690
Ah, right. My bad.

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:22.160
But--!

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:23.310
I'm back!

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:25.300
Rin?!

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:30.550
Damn, you got a whole bag full.

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:31.240
Yup.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:33.120
What's all that?

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:35.210
There's a trade-in back there.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:38.990
But be careful. That clerk always overprices things.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.180
Trade-in?

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:45.080
Yeah. You can trade-in your crappy tags for water and solids and stuff.

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:49.360
Hey, hey.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.900
How 'bout we...

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:56.600
...do something fun together?

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:08.830
Are we going up?

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:20.230
It broke...!

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:21.920
Don't worry!

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:23.580
It's actually very sturdy!

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:24.470
See!

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:27.670
Come on, hurry up!

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:30.400
Okay! We get it! Just chill out!

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:45.950
Nice view.

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.950
I found this place recently on accident.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:52.980
Although this city doesn't seem very interesting at first glance,

00:09:53.870 --> 00:09:55.700
it has a million dollar night view.

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:57.930
Well, not quite a million since it's pretty bad around here, but...

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:01.700
I guess...

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:06.730
I was thinking it'd be nice to see it with the rest of you.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:14.810
So, today is on me!

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:16.570
Let's party!

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:19.750
Really?

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:22.720
Yeah! Don't worry! I've got lots of crap tags!

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.020
Gramps, you like this, right?

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:28.160
Good boy!

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:29.500
Thank you.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:33.710
Oh, green curry! What do you want, Akira?

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:35.030
Whatever.

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:40.910
Akira always eats this one.

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:42.190
More like occasionally.

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:47.490
Hmm, so you like the omelet-rice flavor, huh?

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:49.380
What a surprise! You eat like a little kid!

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:52.580
Who cares what the flavor is.

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:55.620
No way, it's important to be picky!

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:57.860
My favorite is definitely meat!

00:10:57.860 --> 00:10:59.560
Especially the barbecued meat!

00:11:02.530 --> 00:11:06.170
Keisuke, don't you have a
maniacal liking to green curry?

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.040
I dunno...

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.200
It usually tastes good, but...

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.130
That scent is kinda strong.

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:14.280
Eh? I-I'm sorry!

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:16.190
I'll finish it right away!

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:19.760
Lemme have a bite.

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:24.420
Figures. They all taste the same.

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:28.960
Does that mean you think that
one's tasty too? Or is it gross?

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:29.830
It's good!

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:31.470
You have no sense of taste!

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:53.980
Well then...

00:11:56.530 --> 00:11:59.150
I've got some minor business to attend to now.

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:00.550
Thanks for sharin'.

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:04.490
Well, you did seem lonesome over there by yourself.

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:07.220
Later.

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:43.390
You're not coming after me?

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:09.350
Move!

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:10.930
Move it already!

00:13:30.690 --> 00:13:32.640
Don't fuck with me!

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:05.760
Hey.

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:09.180
Have you by any chance done Bl@ster before?

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:14.150
Ah, I thought so!

00:14:14.150 --> 00:14:15.740
As an individual or on a team?

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:17.330
Only as an individual.

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:21.990
I only did team fighting.

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:26.820
I liked the previous version of Bl@ster better.

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:29.740
We just scrimmaged in the alleyways.

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:31.920
Ah, me too.

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:32.930
Yeah?

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:36.980
We could demonstrate and compare our genuine strengths that way.

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:40.080
I joined because I admired that part.

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:46.380
I guess it was like, I thought I could
find my true friends through fighting.

00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:49.900
After pummeling each other till our guts were almost hollowed out, we'd glare at each other.

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:55.320
We were able to be friends
because of that. It was great!

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.600
I admired those kinds of guys.

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:10.480
You see, I...

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:19.080
I just love that face of yours, Akira!

00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:23.020
H-Hey!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:23.920
Akira!~

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:35.640
Ah, do you feel awkward now?

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:36.460
No!

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:40.010
Eh? What's with you, Akira? What a killjoy.

00:15:40.010 --> 00:15:42.750
Hey Rin, quit playing around!

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:44.350
Then how 'bout we get serious?

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:46.140
Don't mess with me! Get off!

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:07.330
It's Shiki!

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:14.740
S-Shiki's here!!!

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:22.060
What's the matter-- Rin?!

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:43.000
Sounds like Shiki appeared in
the northern part of District 6.

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:44.340
Hey, isn't that close?!

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:46.400
The whole surface of that area is a sea of blood.

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:47.340
For real?

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:48.000
What are we gonna do?!

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:50.960
Well, Shiki won't dare lay a hand on this place.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:03.150
Shiki... Just who is he?

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:09.960
Rin?!

00:18:04.030 --> 00:18:05.610
You're that trash from before, huh?

00:18:46.630 --> 00:18:47.720
That all you got?

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:51.490
Don't screw with me!

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:20.860
You still brandish your sword
though you know you can't win.

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:26.490
It seems as though you really want to die.

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:36.670
I'll grant you that wish.

00:19:53.820 --> 00:19:54.900
J-Just...

00:19:58.140 --> 00:19:59.190
Kill me already.

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:05.400
Trying to be pushy even though you're the loser?

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:09.300
Dogs should be like dogs and just bark.

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:19.500
If you were to cry and beg for forgiveness,

00:20:21.510 --> 00:20:23.700
I may change my mind about killing you.

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:40.650
What arrogant eyes you have.

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:03.160
As if I'd beg for my life...

00:21:16.310 --> 00:21:18.570
I'll play with you again when I feel like it.

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:55.300
So that's...

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:57.080
...Shiki...

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:14.620
Now the moon and the clouding darkness of the night

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:14.620
Tsuki to Kageru Yain Ima wa

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:18.390
tempts the corrupt world

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:18.390
Kegareta Sekai wo Izanau

00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:22.130
At our hanging bonds,

00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:22.130
Tsurirareta Kizuna ni wa

00:22:22.130 --> 00:22:28.750
the melody of sadness will never end

00:22:22.130 --> 00:22:28.750
Kanashiki Shirabe Owaranai

00:22:37.140 --> 00:22:40.650
Our raging hearts burst open

00:22:37.140 --> 00:22:40.650
Areteta Kokoro wa Sakete

00:22:40.930 --> 00:22:44.130
Entangled with irrationality and reflection,

00:22:40.930 --> 00:22:44.130
Karamiau Futou to Kage

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:48.150
we become aware of our hidden actions

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:48.150
Kakusareta Koudou ga Mezame

00:22:48.260 --> 00:22:51.330
My own coldheartedness caresses my skin

00:22:49.600 --> 00:22:51.330
Reiketsu ga Hada wo Naderu

00:22:51.670 --> 00:22:53.350
Whilst possessing a barrier,

00:22:51.670 --> 00:22:53.350
Kekkai wo Motsubi

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:55.160
it's a history of fright!

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:55.160
Kyougaku no HISTORY

00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:58.470
I'm being driven into the corner

00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:58.470
Oitsumereta Koudou wa

00:22:58.930 --> 00:23:00.750
by the stiffening

00:22:58.930 --> 00:23:00.750
Sakimidareru

00:23:00.750 --> 00:23:02.620
rust in full bloom

00:23:00.750 --> 00:23:02.620
Sabi wo Koru

00:23:02.620 --> 00:23:06.750
and his red eye sees

00:23:02.620 --> 00:23:06.750
Akai Hitomi wo

00:23:07.610 --> 00:23:11.720
Now the moon and the clouding darkness of the night

00:23:07.610 --> 00:23:11.720
Tsuki to Kageru Yain Ima wa

00:23:11.720 --> 00:23:15.550
tempts the corrupt world

00:23:11.720 --> 00:23:15.550
Kegareta Sekai wo Izanau

00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:18.860
At our hanging bonds,

00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:18.860
Tsurirareta Kizuna ni wa

00:23:19.260 --> 00:23:22.210
the melody of sadness plays

00:23:19.260 --> 00:23:22.210
Kanashiki Shirabe

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:26.320
The tears of our cage and our lips

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:26.320
Ano Kuchibiru Namida wa

00:23:26.590 --> 00:23:30.280
leave behind our intersecting love

00:23:26.590 --> 00:23:30.280
Majiwaru Ai wo Inokoru

00:23:30.490 --> 00:23:33.670
To not hurry along the future,

00:23:30.490 --> 00:23:33.670
Saki Sekasenaku ni wa

00:23:34.110 --> 00:23:40.580
the rusty thorn does not hesitate

00:23:34.110 --> 00:23:40.580
Sabitsuita Toge Mayowanai

00:23:50.500 --> 00:23:52.400
Hah? What is it, old man?

00:23:52.400 --> 00:23:53.430
An information shop?

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:55.280
If you don't have any tags, get outta my sight.

00:23:56.370 --> 00:23:59.570
If you don't gain anything by knowing
someone, you'll just get betrayed quickly.

00:23:59.570 --> 00:24:01.650
Think of yourself as being cuter than everyone else.

00:24:01.620 --> 00:24:04.250
Episode 5

00:24:01.650 --> 00:24:03.990
Those who believe in others are idiots.
